==Restrictions==
Rarity: Only [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare]]

==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 6.67~16.67 seconds<sup>200f~500f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Heavenly Hippoe]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 23.33~33.33 seconds<sup>700f~1,000f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Divine Cyclone]] spawns as the boss.
**1 [[Angel Fanboy]] spawns.
**3 [[Gabriel]]s spawn, delay 0.67~1.33 seconds<sup>20f~40f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Gabriel]]s spawn, delay 13.33~23.33 seconds<sup>400f~700f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The restriction forces you to rely on either [[Stilts Cat (Rare Cat)|Totem Cat]] or [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]] to stall the boss. For a meatshield, [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Artist Cat]] or [[Pogo Cat (Rare Cat)|Jiangshi Cat]] is recommended. If you somehow don't have these units, then you're at the mercy of the [[Cat Capsule|Rare Cat Capsule]] to give you what you need for this stage.

==Trivia==
*Although its English name starts with a "D", Divine Cyclone appears in stages called [[Wrath of A-Cyclone (Insane)|Wrath of A-Cyclone]] and [[Revenge of A-Cyclone (Deadly)|Revenge of A-Cyclone]]. This is likely attributable to poor localization, since [[Divine Cyclone]]'s Japanese name is Angel Cyclone.

